Third-party components

Textual bundles or links against third-party components that are distributed
under their own licenses. These licenses apply to those components only and
are not superseded by the license above. Notable examples:

   * The Blowfish Encryption extension contains code licensed under the
     GNU General Public License, version 2. See
     "Sources/Plugins/Blowfish Encryption/LICENSE-GPLv2.txt".
   * The Encryption Kit framework links libotr, libgcrypt, libgpg-error,
     and OTRKit, which are licensed under the GNU Lesser General Public
     License.
   * Bundled styles include their own copyright and license files.

See the "Third-party software" section of README.md and Acknowledgements.pdf
for the complete list of components, their licenses, and their copyright
holders.
